-- title:
--   Auxiliary prime: rank at most twice the base rank
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V=2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$, and $N\ge 1$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid N$, $p\nmid r-1$, and such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $r\in P^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ (i.e. $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup and acts as $x\mapsto x^{r}$ on the residue field of $P$) one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\ne (r+1)^2$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every $P$ lying over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Assume finally the two commutativity hypotheses: the operators $\mathrm{heckeTL}_{\ell}$ on [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) indexed by the generator set `Gen N r S` commute pairwise (`BaseOpComm`), and likewise the operators `op N r S 𝒪 g` on `Carrier N r 𝒪` commute pairwise (`OpComm`). Then the $\mathcal O$-rank of the module `ML` attached to the auxiliary-level Hecke data (carrier `Carrier N r 𝒪`, generators `Gen N r S`, operators `op`, residual system $g\mapsto\theta(T_{g.\ell})$) is at most twice the $\mathcal O$-rank of the module `baseML` attached to the corresponding data on [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162).
--
--   This is one half — the upper bound — of the comparison, at an auxiliary Taylor–Wiles prime $r$ satisfying the non-congruence conditions $p\nmid r-1$ and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\ne(r+1)^2$, between the $\theta$-localised cohomology at auxiliary level $r$ and two copies of the same localisation at level $N$; the reverse inequality comes from Ihara's lemma. It is used by [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.exists_linearEquiv_baseML_prod_ML`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.exists_linearEquiv_baseML_prod_ML) to produce the linear isomorphism with a product of two copies of `baseML`.
